1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,880
This is Trigun.

2
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:33,540
Oh, my God.

3
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:41,841
We really do appreciate
you lending us a bus bear.

4
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:43,290
Hmm?

5
00:01:43,373 --> 00:01:44,948
What are you talking about?

6
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:47,677
If we don't come with
you, we can't do our job!

7
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:48,640
I'll hate you!

8
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:52,437
I'll haunt you and your children
and your children's children, too!

9
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:56,057
Oh yeah, I knew it was a mistake,
but I couldn't take the whining.

10
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:56,977
I appreciate it!

11
00:01:57,060 --> 00:02:00,617
Okay, okay, you can shower me with
all the appreciation you want.

12
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:03,057
Just make sure you pay
me back when we hit town.

13
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:04,611
My wallet's almost empty.

14
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:06,251
You've got a point there.

15
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:09,652
Am I really getting through to this girl?

16
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:11,157
I'm a little bit thirsty.

17
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:13,217
Do you think that I can
have some of your water?

18
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:15,517
I'm not getting through to her at all.

19
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:16,894
Will you keep it down?

20
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,637
Haven't you noticed that
everyone here is exhausted

21
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,277
from the terrible ordeal
in the sand steamer?

22
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:24,097
Don't worry, I've shut him up for you.

23
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:26,356
He won't be causing any more trouble.

24
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:29,595
I really don't think you had to hit me

25
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:48,800
That is one heck of a
well-prepared dead guy

26
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:52,820
Hey you

27
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:55,077
Ha! Ahem.

28
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:56,297
Well, praise the Lord.

29
00:02:56,380 --> 00:02:57,210
Hello!

30
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,360
Are you all right?

31
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:06,940
Here, have some water.

32
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:08,400
Oh, thank you.

33
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:16,020
Ah, I'm alive again!

34
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,940
I'm much obliged. You're welcome.

35
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,620
But that was my...

36
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:24,277
What were you doing out in
the middle of the desert?

37
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:25,190
Well,

38
00:03:25,273 --> 00:03:28,357
my bike decided to break down on me about
100 aisles or so down the road from here,

39
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,997
so I thought I'd just hoof it.

40
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:32,757
Are you saying you
actually walked 100 aisles?

41
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:33,670
That's right.

42
00:03:33,753 --> 00:03:35,073
It was pretty horrible.

43
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:42,637
Gee, it must have been awfully tiring to
walk carrying that huge thing on your back.

44
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:44,137
I couldn't leave it behind.

45
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:46,220
I do have my pride as a tradesman.

46
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:47,610
A tradesman?

47
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:50,060
I'm a man of the cloth. You?

48
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:51,201
Are you serious?

49
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:54,240
Do you like make pretty dresses? Hardly.

50
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:57,077
I'm a priest saving the lambs
who have strayed off their path.

51
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,219
A soldier of love!

52
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,377
You girls are the ones who
spotted me, aren't you?

53
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:03,660
You saved my life. Well, actually,

54
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:05,357
the one that spotted you
when you were nothing but a

55
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:08,675
tiny little speck on the
horizon was that pathetic guy.

56
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:12,020
Oh. Hey!

57
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:14,097
I'm alive because of what you did!

58
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:15,768
How could I ever thank you?

59
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:22,000
I am known as Valentines
Alcalinella Zijak Shushirabo Heretz.

60
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:28,560
Gumbi Gobella, Blue Stradivari, Talent
Trent Pierre, Andre Chartenhamos,

61
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:33,660
Yvato Vinci Baldos George,
Deutzel Kaiser III.

62
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,413
Don't hesitate to call.

63
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:38,080
What are you talking about, Mr.

64
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:39,260
Bash the Stampede?

65
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,740
I hate it when you call
me by my full name!

66
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:44,600
The Vash?

67
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:47,329
You mean to say he's
THE Vash the Stampede?

68
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,420
Can this man really be him?

69
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:55,522
He's absolutely nothing
at all like I envisioned.

70
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:57,360
How's that possible?

71
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,940
Yeah, I know I have
trouble believing it too.

72
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:01,997
You mean...

73
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:04,500
Oh, hey, gee, sorry about that.

74
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:10,080
I'm Wolfwood, at your service.

75
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:17,200
Life sure can be funny sometimes.

76
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:21,365
Imagine running into the legendary
alcohol in a place like this.

77
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:25,237
Don't broadcast it to
the whole world, okay?

78
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:28,617
If I shot you dead right now and
collected the 60 billion double dollars,

79
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:31,171
I'd have a really fun journey, wouldn't I?

80
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,725
I weren't listening, were you?

81
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:35,120
Got any more water?

82
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:37,005
I would, but you drank it all.

83
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:38,553
Yeah, sorry about that.

84
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:45,617
Hey, they seem to be
getting along really well.

85
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:48,465
The birds of the feather
have flocked together.

86
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:51,880
That was a long trip.

87
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:53,460
I gotta go sleep.

88
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:55,240
I gotta stretch.

89
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:59,047
Look, mister, do me a favor.

90
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:00,897
Please count it one more time.

91
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:02,180
Okay, ready?

92
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:07,360
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

93
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:09,197
Recount it all you want.

94
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:10,177
It's still not enough.

95
00:06:10,260 --> 00:06:13,417
Like I told you, the fare is
one hundred double dollars.

96
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:15,357
If I give you any more,
I'll die of starvation.

97
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:17,852
Come on, driver, please, give me a break.

98
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:19,810
Uh...

99
00:06:19,893 --> 00:06:20,723
All right, I'll tell you what.

100
00:06:20,806 --> 00:06:22,217
I'll let you ride for
eighty double dollars.

101
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:23,130
Take it or leave it.

102
00:06:23,213 --> 00:06:24,043
Really?

103
00:06:24,126 --> 00:06:25,180
That'd be great! Thanks a lot!

104
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:26,896
Oh, I almost forgot!

105
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:28,370
Whoa!

106
00:06:28,453 --> 00:06:29,637
Whoa, what the hell is this?

107
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:30,697
It's a confessional.

108
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:33,917
You know, those private rooms they
used to have in the churches back home?

109
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,300
This one is portable.

110
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:39,517
You must have something to confess
some blasphemous act and indiscretion.

111
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:40,877
Maybe it's on the house.

112
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:42,380
Go ahead. Don't be shy

113
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:46,277
No, thanks Padre.

114
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:50,600
Huh well now he's not much fun Looks
like you've got a pretty tough job.

115
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:51,570
Hmm.

116
00:06:51,653 --> 00:06:52,917
Is that thing part of your gospel?

117
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:53,920
Of course not.

118
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:55,180
It's all business

119
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:56,810
Unfortunately

120
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:05,197
Our church kind of doubles as an orphanage
we scrape out a living doing what we can

121
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:07,017
we taken all these kids with no living

122
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:11,897
family no place to go
guess it was time I left

123
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:15,257
the church anyway I
decided it was a hopeless

124
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:16,737
effort unless I made some money for them

125
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:19,377
are you saying you make money as a priest

126
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:22,700
well I I wouldn't
exactly put it like that,

127
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:23,840
but...

128
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:26,000
Mama, I'm really hungry.

129
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,220
And tired.

130
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:29,417
We'll be in the city sooner
than you think, girls,

131
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:31,417
and once we get there, I'll
give you plenty to eat.

132
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:33,088
Be patient for Mommy, okay?

133
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:34,377
But Mom...

134
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:36,020
Don't be that way, honey.

135
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,454
It's only gonna be a little bit longer.

136
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:44,900
I want food now!

137
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:45,850
Mama, I'm thirsty!

138
00:07:45,933 --> 00:07:46,763
Please, Mama!

139
00:07:46,846 --> 00:07:47,676
Are you guys hungry?

140
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:50,960
Uh-huh. I see.

141
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:52,500
Well, I have these.

142
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:55,309
They're little, but
they taste pretty good.

143
00:07:58,920 --> 00:07:59,750
Okay.

144
00:07:59,833 --> 00:08:01,720
Well, this is yours.

145
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:04,300
And this one is yours.

146
00:08:04,680 --> 00:08:08,060
And then this one, uh, is mine.

147
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:11,931
Sorry it's not much, but you
think it'll be enough for now?

148
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:24,380
Thank you.

149
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:28,000
Come on, you two.

150
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:29,257
Wasn't that nice?

151
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:30,170
Yeah!

152
00:08:30,253 --> 00:08:31,083
I woke up a crumb!

153
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:38,200
Well, I'll be.

154
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:41,197
I'm actually surprised that
you can smile like that.

155
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:42,110
Huh?

156
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:43,257
What do you mean?

157
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:44,928
You had me kind of worried.

158
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:48,117
I noticed that you always
smile and seem really friendly,

159
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:51,612
But the way you smiled was so
empty, it hurt to watch you.

160
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:56,222
You're hurting like crazy on the
inside, yet you grin and bear it.

161
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,471
At least that's this man's opinion anyway.

162
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:03,000
That's why I have this confessional!

163
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:06,637
No matter what the
worry, I'll listen to it.

164
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:08,132
Just put a coin in here.

165
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:09,957
You're really good at your trade.

166
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,617
I've got to be to make a living.

167
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:13,112
It's not easy, you know.

168
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:14,776
Somebody come quick!

169
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,397
Eric is completely crazy!

170
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:18,380
I guess it was bound to happen.

171
00:09:18,820 --> 00:09:20,340
The sun is getting worse

172
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:24,898
Hey, Eric, buddy, are you all right?

173
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:25,900
Hang on, okay?

174
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:27,817
It was...

175
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:28,880
Don't talk.

176
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,957
Hey, get the stretcher over here.

177
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,157
He's just falling down.

178
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:34,064
He doesn't really look that bad

179
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:40,548
There isn't anyone here,
but the passengers.

180
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:49,157
Now why are you pointing that thing at me?

181
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:50,357
Well, it was you, wasn't it?

182
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:53,217
It was no mortal that did
this. Huh? Come again?

183
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:56,997
What the hell is that?

184
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,240
That thing is huge.

185
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:07,577
Well, it's still alive.

186
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:08,490
What is it?

187
00:10:08,573 --> 00:10:12,817
Hey?

188
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:14,140
Not bad, girl.

189
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:22,140
Why doesn't anything nice ever follow you?

190
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:24,459
I know, it's a real drag, isn't it?

191
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,397
What the hell are those ugly things?

192
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,737
Hunts of lost technology?

193
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:31,650
Damn!

194
00:10:31,733 --> 00:10:34,797
It's all because I changed my route
to save that stupid cheap priest.

195
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:35,710
I'm too nice.

196
00:10:35,793 --> 00:10:37,137
I should have charged him full price.

197
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:38,050
Get down now.

198
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,797
How can they still be operational?

199
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:45,351
Their expiration date was a long time ago.

200
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:47,520
This is horrible.

201
00:10:48,180 --> 00:10:49,180
Can you help him?

202
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:51,137
I may not look it, but I am a priest.

203
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:52,102
Leave it to me.

204
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:54,106
I'm sure I have a book on it.

205
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:59,600
Never mind. I'll do it. Okay, thanks.

206
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,070
Helen?

207
00:11:03,153 --> 00:11:04,307
Has anyone seen my daughter?

208
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,320
Oh, my God, no.

209
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:14,160
Take care of the wounded man! Oh, dear!

210
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:26,238
What are you doing?

211
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:28,604
Don't ask ridiculous questions.

212
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:30,331
I'm gonna save the child.

213
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:31,655
With your bare hands?

214
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:35,800
Oh, shit!

215
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:39,822
You would have gone anyway, huh?

216
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,260
Of course I would.

217
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,075
I see him, I see him.

218
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:04,997
There's lots of those big guys.

219
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:09,256
Hey, I bet those are nothing for the
likes of Vash the Stampede, right?

220
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,334
What's wrong with you?

221
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:12,837
My stomach kinda hurts.

222
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:14,897
Aw, come on now, tough guy, get over it.

223
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:16,417
You're not that fragile, are you?

224
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:20,147
I got shot by the leader of the
Bad Lads about three days ago.

225
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:22,831
You got shot by Brilliant Dynamite's Neon.

226
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:24,653
Now that is impressive.

227
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:27,682
You do lead an exciting
life, just like they say.

228
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:28,630
We gotta go.

229
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,817
You listen to people,
and then again you don't.

230
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:31,730
What's up with that?

231
00:12:31,813 --> 00:12:33,397
A child's life is on the line.

232
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:34,310
She needs help.

233
00:12:34,393 --> 00:12:36,217
Just look for a second, will ya?

234
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:40,300
They use that thing on the end to
detect objects which radiate heat.

235
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:42,380
Hey, listen to me!

236
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:45,920
I don't have time to just
sit around and chit-chat.

237
00:12:51,620 --> 00:12:52,820
Oh, this is bad.

238
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:54,357
This is gonna be tough.

239
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,380
I'm in trouble!

240
00:12:57,300 --> 00:12:59,580
Your ID has not been registered.

241
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:02,254
Therefore, you may not enter this area.

242
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:05,840
You will now be removed by force.

243
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:15,130
Get down!

244
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:16,710
Fire!

245
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:24,354
That's him, all of it.

246
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:25,760
Hey, nice support!

247
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:27,860
And you were a nice decoy.

248
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:30,570
Oh!

249
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:35,197
Now that's what's known as a nice cover.

250
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:36,977
You were the decoy that time.

251
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:37,890
Huh, guess so.

252
00:13:37,973 --> 00:13:38,803
Nice support.

253
00:13:40,700 --> 00:13:41,530
What is it?

254
00:13:41,613 --> 00:13:42,443
Over there!

255
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:51,895
She's still alive, and she looks okay.

256
00:13:51,980 --> 00:13:52,921
Praise the Lord!

257
00:13:58,700 --> 00:13:59,640
He's fast.

258
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:01,180
Unbelievably fast.

259
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:03,499
That sounded like a single gunshot.

260
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:11,480
Thanks a lot, Bash.

261
00:14:15,820 --> 00:14:19,860
Well, it looks like we're
just about done, huh? Nuts!

262
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:37,170
No!

263
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:41,280
No! No! No! No! No!

264
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,944
What an embarrassing way to go.

265
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:50,700
What is this place?

266
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:52,808
We really fell into it now.

267
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:54,697
We're smack in the middle
of their territory.

268
